# HTML BASIC NOTES

## 1. What is HTML?
HTML stands for HyperText Markup Language. It is used to create web pages.

## 2. Basic HTML Structure
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My First Website</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hello World</h1>
    <p>Welcome to HTML</p>
</body>
</html>
```

## 3. Important HTML Tags

- `<html>` – Defines the HTML document.
- `<head>` – Contains page information.
- `<title>` – Sets the page title.
- `<body>` – Contains visible content.
- `<h1>` – Creates a main heading.
- `<p>` – Creates a paragraph.
- `<br>` – Inserts a line break.
- `<hr>` – Creates a horizontal line.
- `<b>` – Makes text bold.
- `<i>` – Makes text italic.
- `<u>` – Underlines text.

## 4. Example 1: Simple Web Page
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>My Page</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Welcome</h1>
    <p>This is my first HTML page.</p>
</body>
</html>
```

## 5. Example 2: Heading, Button and Link
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>HTML Basics</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Hello World!</h1>
    <h2>About Me</h2>
    <p>I am learning HTML.</p>
    <button>Click Me</button>
    <br><br>
    <a href="https://www.google.com">Visit Google</a>
</body>
</html>
```

## 6. How to Run HTML
1. Open Notepad.
2. Type or paste the HTML code.
3. Save the file as `index.html`.
4. Open the file in Google Chrome.

## 7. Advantages of HTML
1. Easy to learn and use.
2. Creates web page structures.
3. Supported by web browsers.
4. Works with CSS and JavaScript.
5. Free
